      "math_academy_id": "q-225082",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(4.9)$ given below, compute $P(X>8).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.4582\\,$ | $\\,0.6335\\,$ | $\\,0.7767\\,$ | $\\,0.8769\\,$ | $\\,0.9382\\,$ | $\\,0.9717\\,$ | $\\,0.9880\\,$ |\n\n$P(X>8)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>8) & =1-P(X\\le 8) \\\\  & =1-F(8) \\\\  & =1-0.9382 \\\\  & =0.0618.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
